{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And He said, you shall ascend, you and Aaron with you.</b> A little above the boundary, so that he not go far from Israel, for they are destined to say to him when HaShem finishes speaking the Ten Commandments: You speak with us and we will hear (Exodus 20:16 below). And I answer him regarding his question: for He did not tell him to warn them lest they see Him, but only lest they cross the boundary, for they need him to warn them at the time of the event, that they hear and guard their souls:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:01.889063024Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}